(C) full truth table of a noisy parity (d=12, n=4096, flips i.i.d. p=1/8): product vs shared class
  flips F=509; -log2 nu_(a,qhat)(D) = 2218.0 (qhat=0.125); log2 C(n,F) = 2212.3; -log2 U(D) = 2234.0
  lambda= 1.0: product-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise)   shared-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise) [J(memo)-J(sampler) = 8.2, J(U)-J(sampler) = 3.8]
  lambda= 1.1: product-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise)   shared-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise) [J(memo)-J(sampler) = 230.9, J(U)-J(sampler) = 2.6]
  lambda= 1.5: product-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise)   shared-class MAP = U (shared mixture)   [J(memo)-J(sampler) = 1121.4, J(U)-J(sampler) = -2.3]
  lambda= 2.0: product-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise)   shared-class MAP = U (shared mixture)   [J(memo)-J(sampler) = 2234.5, J(U)-J(sampler) = -8.3]
  lambda= 3.0: product-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise)   shared-class MAP = U (shared mixture)   [J(memo)-J(sampler) = 4460.8, J(U)-J(sampler) = -20.5]
  lambda= 6.0: product-class MAP = sampler (parity+noise)   shared-class MAP = U (shared mixture)   [J(memo)-J(sampler) = 11139.6, J(U)-J(sampler) = -57.0]
